  "from": "kalshi_series_subjects.v1.json",
  "rule": "A series is listed here when its Wikipedia titles imply EXACTLY ONE tags.v1 subject through the title table below, which is what 'where the two agree' means (ruling R295). A title that determines no facet on its own is absent from that table on purpose: a city, 'Weather forecasting', 'Cryptocurrency', 'United States dollar' and 'Economy of the United States' are all context rather than subject. So a series whose titles imply no subject, and one whose titles imply two, are both left out and their markets are tagged by the keyword rules of tags.v1 from the question text. The SNOW and RAIN series are the worked example: 'Dallas, Weather forecasting' cannot tell snow from temperature, so KXDALSNOWM is not here and 'Snow in Dallas in Jan 2026?' is tagged precipitation from its own question.",
